      {
        "id": 14,
        "title": "DataStore Implementation",
        "description": "Implement DataStore for persistent app settings including session duration, interval time, image availability, and permission status.",
        "details": "1. Create a `data/preferences` package\n2. Define a `PreferencesKeys` object:\n   ```kotlin\n   object PreferencesKeys {\n     val DURATION_MS = longPreferencesKey(\"duration_ms\")\n     val INTERVAL_MS = longPreferencesKey(\"interval_ms\")\n     val HAS_IMAGES = booleanPreferencesKey(\"has_images\")\n     val HAS_PERMISSIONS = booleanPreferencesKey(\"has_permissions\")\n   }\n   ```\n3. Create a `SettingsRepository` interface:\n   ```kotlin\n   interface SettingsRepository {\n     val durationMs: Flow<Long>\n     val intervalMs: Flow<Long>\n     val hasImages: Flow<Boolean>\n     val hasPermissions: Flow<Boolean>\n     \n     suspend fun setDurationMs(durationMs: Long)\n     suspend fun setIntervalMs(intervalMs: Long)\n     suspend fun setHasImages(hasImages: Boolean)\n     suspend fun setHasPermissions(hasPermissions: Boolean)\n   }\n   ```\n4. Implement `SettingsRepositoryImpl` using DataStore\n5. Create a Hilt module to provide the repository:\n   ```kotlin\n   @Module\n   @InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class)\n   object DataStoreModule {\n     @Provides\n     @Singleton\n     fun provideDataStore(@ApplicationContext context: Context): DataStore<Preferences> {\n       return PreferenceDataStoreFactory.create {\n         context.preferencesDataStoreFile(\"nudgr_settings\")\n       }\n     }\n     \n     @Provides\n     @Singleton\n     fun provideSettingsRepository(dataStore: DataStore<Preferences>): SettingsRepository {\n       return SettingsRepositoryImpl(dataStore)\n     }\n   }\n   ```\n6. Create a `SettingsViewModel` that exposes the repository data as LiveData/StateFlow",
        "testStrategy": "1. Write unit tests for `SettingsRepositoryImpl` using a test DataStore\n2. Test each preference key for read/write operations\n3. Verify default values are returned when preferences don't exist\n4. Test the ViewModel exposes the correct data from the repository\n5. Manually test persistence across app restarts",
        "priority": "high",
        "dependencies": [
          13
        ],
        "status": "done",
        "subtasks": []
